at, but can round to e.g. 8 decimals for consistency. Or leave as is. I'll round to 8 decimal places as typical for float representation. Alternatively, we could round to 4? But better to keep as computed. I'll do round(gain, 10) to avoid floating point issues. The fixture doesn't specify. I'll use round(gain, 8). Also ensure output keys exactly as schema.\n\nThe output must be JSON-serializable.\n\nImplementation in Python, using standard library only.\n\nReturn a dict with keys \"accepted_call_ids\" and \"diagnostics\", where accepted_call_ids is list of strings, diagnostics is list of dicts.\n\nNote: the case payload may have extra keys like \"_case_nonce\", but we ignore.\n\nWrite solve function, then wrap in JSON with key \"implementation\". Must escape the source code as JSON string.\n\nLet's produce the code."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":2087,"completion_tokens":605,"total_tokens":2692,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1792},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":431},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1792,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":295},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}